# Make App Fully Database-Driven & Pink Slip Auto-Absent

Replace all mock/hardcoded data in the Flutter app so every piece of displayed information comes from the Supabase cloud database. When an advisor issues a pink slip, automatically mark the student **absent** in the `daily_attendance` table.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This is a large architectural change. The app currently uses **~1300 lines of hardcoded mock data** in `MockDataService` (fake absentee lists, fake leave requests, fake defaulter calculations, fake analytics trends). Replacing all of this with live Supabase queries means:
> - The app will be slower on first load (network calls vs in-memory data)
> - If Supabase is unreachable, the app will show empty/error states instead of mock data
> - Features like "promotion engine", "alumni archive", "academic calendar" will remain client-side since they have no corresponding Supabase tables

> [!WARNING]
> The existing **21 unit tests** rely on `StudentDirectoryData` (the static 622-student directory) and `MockDataService` hardcoded leave requests. Making everything 100% live-database would break all tests since tests don't have network access. The plan preserves `StudentDirectoryData` as the offline fallback and keeps tests working.

## Open Questions

1. **Dates with no attendance data**: The Supabase `daily_attendance` table only has records for Sep 7 and Sep 8 (1244 rows = 622 × 2). For other dates (Sep 1-6, Oct, Nov, Dec), should the app show "No data" or should we seed more attendance data?
2. **Promotion / Alumni / Academic Calendar**: These features have no Supabase tables. Should they remain as client-side logic, or should we create new tables for them?
3. **Defaulter calculation**: Currently uses a fake hash-based formula. Should defaulters be computed from actual `daily_attendance` records (count present/absent per student across all dates)?

